Enable torch.compile for the Kimi-K3 DSpark draft model.

Ported from upstream vLLM PR #56664 (OPEN as of 2026-09-14, author fululi12):
https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/56664

Without @support_torch_compile the DSpark forward graph is never compiled, so
every configured Inductor fusion pass is inert on it. This is the draft model
only -- the Kimi-K3 TARGET is still compile-free, so target-side passes stay
inert either way.

Pairs with COMPILATION_EXTRA_JSON='"use_inductor_graph_partition":true', which
is what actually lets fuse_rope_kvcache_cat_mla resolve to true (see
vllm/config/vllm.py::enable_rope_kvcache_mla_fusion). The decorator alone
compiles the graph; the config alone unlocks the pass. Upstream measured them
together (+6.7% intvty p90 at depth 3 on MI355X) and could not separate them --
our A/B runs the config-only arm first precisely so we can.

--- a/models/kimi_k3/nvidia/dspark_mla.py
+++ b/models/kimi_k3/nvidia/dspark_mla.py
